\title{M-F · Foundation feasibility (new; after M0, before M1)}
\taxon{Milestone}
\meta{id}{M-F}
\meta{origin}{design/08-roadmap.md}
\meta{status}{in-progress}
\tag{milestone}

\p{See \code{11-foundation-feasibility.md} for the exact tests and dependencies.}
\ul{
  \li{Compile the universe signatures and demonstrate a real bundled seal and swap.}
  \li{Repair object reduction and prove the boundary/Segal-core comparison actually used.}
  \li{Establish categorical diagram spaces on ordinary-category examples with natural equivalences, separately from relative presheaf maps.}
  \li{Test and prove the required discrete/general equivalence clauses, including duplicate horizontals, endpoint transport, and 2-out-of-3 in the proposed root setting.}
  \li{Eliminate the unsupported truncation from required interfaces; demonstrate boundary monodromy and a coherent-cell route that retains the needed information.}
  \li{Establish the augmented arities and the actual cofibrancy/replacement machinery used by the prototype; prove the no-horizontal 2-category comparison.}
  \li{Construct relative monads/modules and one small nondiscrete matrix/Mod example, including whole-object fibres and the natural-equivalence extraction.}
  \li{Check the corrected symmetry ambient on a discrete action example; scope pasting and rectification accurately; pass the compiled-dependency and axiom audits.}
}
\p{\strong{Exit:} \ref{at-fd-0001} through \ref{at-fd-0011} passed: mathematical components have checked proofs of their current statements with approved axioms, and tooling components have reproducible check records. No blocked prerequisite is hidden behind a later milestone. A gate may be revised only with a decision explaining the change and its impact. Failed gates keep the dependent foundation provisional. There is no “all gates passed” status in this document revision: the remaining gates are open.}
\p{\strong{Freeze:} only the successfully validated minimal presentation/API fragment. Full root and interface freeze remains \ref{ms-0003}, with the required \ref{ms-foundation} results as prerequisites.}

\p{\em{Current evidence:} the first work item is checked: \ref{at-kr-0000}, minimal universe signatures under \ref{at-fd-0001}, the scoped nonempty seal under \ref{at-fd-0002}, and small ordinary category/groupoid examples. Work is now on \ref{at-fd-0007}: incidence, the ordinary-active obstruction and a supplied 2-category's binary cell model are checked; \ref{augmented-algebra} adds the equation families, complete-boundary proofs and a nontrivial lawful model. \ref{augmented-transport} adds shape/label separation, explicit transport equations, strict 2-category extraction and reverse operation data. The reverse algebra laws, comparison round trips and discrete nerve, free/arity presentation and labelled diagram-model lemmas remain open. No full foundation completion or root freeze is claimed.}
